From: Jan Równicki <jan@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: log port link clocks

Wave 7 reaches PHY link-up but its SGMII PCS does not assert link status.
Log the requested and effective PPE port RX/TX clock rates after speed
configuration so the failing Linux state can be compared with the working
vendor firmware.

This is diagnostic-only.

Signed-off-by: Jan Równicki <jan@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
@@ -807,6 +807,12 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	dev_info(device,
+		 "PPE port %d link clock: interface=%s speed=%d requested=%lu rx=%lu tx=%lu\n",
+		 ppe_port->port_id, phy_modes(interface), speed, rate,
+		 clk_get_rate(ppe_port->clks[PPE_PORT_CLK_RST_RX]),
+		 clk_get_rate(ppe_port->clks[PPE_PORT_CLK_RST_TX]));
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
